or&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/vector/resize\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>resize</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  changes the number of elements stored <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function of <code>std::vector&lt;T,Allocator&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/vector/swap\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>swap</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  swaps the contents <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function of <code>std::vector&lt;T,Allocator&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <h5 id=\"vector.3Cbool.3E_specific_modifiers\"><code>vector&lt;bool&gt;</code> specific modifiers </h5>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/vector_bool/flip\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>flip</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  flips all the bits <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/vector_bool/swap\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>swap</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-cmark\">[static]</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  swaps two <code>std::vector&lt;bool&gt;::</code><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/vector_bool/reference\"><code>reference</code>s</a> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public static member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Non-member_functions\">Non-member functions</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/vector/operator_cmp\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>operator==</span><span>operator!=</span><span>operator&lt;</span><span>operator&lt;=</span><span>operator&gt;</span><span>operator&gt;=</span><span>operator&lt;=&gt;</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx20\">(removed in C++20)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx20\">(removed in C++20)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx20\">(removed in C++20)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx20\">(removed in C++20)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx20\">(removed in C++20)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  lexicographically compares the values of two <code>vector</code>s <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/vector/swap2\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>std::swap<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::vector)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  specializes the <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/swap\">std::swap</a></span> algorithm <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/vector/erase2\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>erase<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::vector)</span></span><span>erase_if<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::vector)</span></span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  erases all elements satisfying specific criteria <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Helper_classes\">Helper classes</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/vector_bool/hash\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>std::hash<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">&lt;std::vector&lt;bool&gt;&gt;</span></span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  hash support for <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span></span><strong class=\"selflink\"><code>vector</code></strong><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">bool</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template specialization)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Deduction_guides_.28C.2B.2B17.29\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/vector/deduction_guides\">Deduction guides</a> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(C++17)</span></h3>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>If the size of the bitset is known at compile time, <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/bitset\">std::bitset</a></span> may be used, which offers a richer set of member functions. In addition, <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.boost.org/doc/libs/release/libs/dynamic_bitset/dynamic_bitset.html\" data-external=\"1\"><code>boost::dynamic_bitset</code></a> exists as an alternative to <span><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span></span><code>vector</code><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">bool</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></span>.\n</p><p>Since its representation may be optimized, <span><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span></span><code>vector</code><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">bool</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></span> does not necessarily meet all <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/Container\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">Container</em></a> or <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/SequenceContainer\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">SequenceContainer</em></a> requirements. For example, because <span><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span></span><code>vector</code><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">bool</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">iterator</span></span></span> is implementation-defined, it may not satisfy the <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/ForwardIterator\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">LegacyForwardIterator</em></a> requirement. Use of algorithms such as <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/search\">std::search</a></span> that require <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/ForwardIterator\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">LegacyForwardIterator</em>s</a> may result in <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.boost.org/doc/libs/release/libs/dynamic_bitset/dynamic_bitset.html#rationale\" data-external=\"1\">either compile-time or run-time errors</a>.\n</p><p>The <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.boost.org/doc/libs/release/doc/html/boost/container/vector.html\" data-external=\"1\">Boost.Container version of <code>vector</code></a> does not specialize for <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">bool</span></span>.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable ftm-begin ftm-has-value\">\n<tr>\n<th><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/feature_test\">Feature-test</a> macro\n</th>\n<th><abbr>Value</abbr>\n</th>\n<th><abbr>Std</abbr>\n</th>\n<th>Feature\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/feature_test#cpp_lib_containers_ranges\"><code>__cpp_lib_containers_ranges</code></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/compiler_support/23#cpp_lib_containers_ranges_202202L\"><code>202202L</code></a></td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark\">(C++23)</span></td>\n<td>Ranges construction and insertion for containers\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: no example </div>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue2187\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 2187</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++11\n</td>\n<td>specializations for <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">bool</span></span> lacked <code>emplace</code> and <code>emplace_back</code> member functions\n</td>\n<td>added\n</td></tr></table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Member types","id":"Member_types"},{"depth":3,"text":"Member functions","id":"Member_functions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Non-member functions","id":"Non-member_functions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Helper classes","id":"Helper_classes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Deduction guides (C++17)","id":"Deduction_guides_.28C.2B.2B17.29"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"container","title":"Containers library"}],"children":[{"path":"container/vector_bool/flip","title":"std::vector<bool,Allocator>::flip"},{"path":"container/vector_bool/hash","title":"std::hash<std::vector<bool>>"},{"path":"container/vector_bool/reference","title":"std::vector<bool, Alloc>::reference"},{"path":"container/vector_bool/swap","title":"std::vector<bool,Allocator>::swap"}],"map":{"label":"std::vector<bool>","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. std::vector<bool> is a possibly space-efficient specialization of std::vector for the type bool."},{"label":"Member types","children":[{"label":"value_type","note":"bool"},{"label":"allocator_type","note":"Allocator"},{"label":"size_type","note":"implementation-defined"},{"label":"difference_type","note":"implementation-defined"},{"label":"reference","note":"proxy class representing a reference to a single bool"},{"label":"const_reference","note":"bool"},{"label":"pointer","note":"implementation-defined"},{"label":"+5 more"}]},{"label":"Member functions","children":[{"label":"(constructor)","note":"constructs the vector"},{"label":"(destructor)","note":"destructs the vector"},{"label":"operator=","note":"assigns values to the container"},{"label":"assign","note":"assigns values to the container"},{"label":"assign_range","note":"assigns a range of values to the container"},{"label":"get_allocator","note":"returns the associated allocator"},{"label":"at","note":"access specified element with bounds checking"},{"label":"+25 more"}]},{"label":"Non-member functions","children":[{"label":"operator==, operator!=, operator<, …","note":"lexicographically compares the values of two vectors"},{"label":"std::swap(std::vector)","note":"specializes the std::swap algorithm"},{"label":"erase(std::vector), erase_if(std::vector)","note":"erases all elements satisfying specific criteria"}]},{"label":"Helper classes","children":[{"label":"std::hash<std::vector<bool>>","note":"hash support for std::vector<bool>"}]},{"label":"Deduction guides (C++17)"},{"label":"Notes","note":"If the size of the bitset is known at compile time, std::bitset may be used, which offers a richer set of member functions."},{"label":"Example"}]},"standards":["C++11","C++17","C++20","C++23"],"wordCount":738,"codeBlockCount":0}
